# Bulk run artifacts stay untracked (CLAUDE.md; experiment plan Appendix A);
# summaries and verdicts are committed in the task and experiment reports.
# Without this line `git status --porcelain` is never empty while runs/
# exists, so every record this directory produces would stamp
# `tree_git_dirty: true` and the clean-tree stamp could never be reached
# (the same line as MDA_partitioning_experiment_v2/ and _v3/).
runs/
# The repository-root .gitignore ignores *.dat, which would silently skip
# the 42 tabulated-data files of the PROCESS copy under PROCESS/process/
# (A46 (process-copy) had to stage them with `git add -f`).  Re-include
# them here so a plain `git add` sees them and the copy-identity gate's
# file-set comparison is not the only thing standing between a missing
# data file and a committed copy.
!*.dat
# `!*.dat` above does not cover the committed input files: gitignore matching
# is case-sensitive, the root .gitignore ignores `*.DAT` as well as `*.dat`,
# and the input files are `<configuration>.IN.DAT`.  Without this line
# `git check-ignore -v harness/data/*.IN.DAT` reports `.gitignore:52:*.DAT`
# and the three committed input files can only be staged with `git add -f` --
# which is exactly the shape of an artifact that silently fails to be
# committed.  Scoped to the data directory so that a run output written
# outside `runs/` is still ignored.
!harness/data/*.IN.DAT
